                  "Perceived risk, on the other hand, had no real effect on acceptance. People who saw crypto as high risk did not accept it any less, contrary to what the team expected. Their reading is that this group tolerates risk more than most, and that the value they see may simply drown the risk out. That runs against several earlier studies where risk held people back.",
